Ripple of the 3.3V and 6V power supply were tested. The ripple of the 12V power supply was not tested, as the 12V power comes from an off the shelf power supply that plugs into the wall, and
therefore was not created by us. The ripple of the 3.3V power supply was found to be 135 mV and the ripple of the 6V power supply was 280 mV. This is within our tolerance of 500mV, so 
the buck converter power supplies pass the power subsystem verification. Images from the oscilloscope are shown in figures 9 and 10. 
